The `print_digit` function takes an integer `x` as input and prints the digit 1. The `sys.argv` list contains the arguments passed to the Python interpreter. The `if __name__ == "__main__":` block ensures that the `main` function is only executed when the script is run directly, not when it is imported as a module.

